# L §7.6 item 2 (tally 2.1.6, issue #89): a declared index holds at most 1 000 000 keys; 1..1000001 is LOAD-LIMIT,
# counted before its keys are built. tally 2.1.5's refcore built it and answered 1 000 001. (The edge, 1..1000000,
# answers 1 000 000 but costs seconds here; T's vectors hold it.)
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ns = 1..1000001

ask n: max(pos(k) for k in ns)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LIMIT index ns holds more than 1 000 000 keys (m.tally:9)
